%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5976006531153724f8306a1fd441aa0c, type: 3}
  m_Name: Dispatch_Side_PumpHouse
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: RobotRescue.Runtime::RobotRescue.Narrative.DispatchScript
  lines:
  - cue: intro
    text: 'PIP, the Brightwater pump house flooded and Pebble, the little tide-gauge bot, is stuck across the sump. Three rooms. Take your time: your battery only drains while you move. Stuck? Press H for a hint. Messed up a room? Stand on its red reset pad.'
    duration: 12
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: cell_grabbed
    text: Power cell! It's heavy, it's portable, and it keeps whatever charge you give it.
    duration: 4
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: cell_full
    text: All four bars! That cell's full.
    duration: 3
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: cell_not_full
    text: 'That cradle wants a FULL cell. Count the bars: this one isn''t full yet.'
    duration: 4
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: door1_open
    text: The cradle's powering the door. You moved power further than your cable reaches. That's the whole trick.
    duration: 6
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: gate_partial
    text: The gate moved! A bit. The needle shows how much weight is in the pan. It wants more.
    duration: 5
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: gate_open
    text: Gate's up, and it stays up while the weight stays in. You don't have to hold it.
    duration: 5
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: bridge_partial
    text: The drawbridge is coming down... and stopping halfway. Not enough weight yet.
    duration: 5
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: bridge_open
    text: Bridge is down! Go get Pebble.
    duration: 3
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: pebble_grabbed
    text: Pebble's clinging on. Gently, gently. The tide gauge is by the exit.
    duration: 4
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: pebble_home
    text: Pebble's home! Listen to those pumps. The water's going down already.
    duration: 6
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: room_reset
    text: Room reset. Everything in here is back where it started. Nothing else changed.
    duration: 4
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: hint_available
    text: Hmm, tricky one. If you want a nudge, press H. Each press tells you a little more.
    duration: 5
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: hint_solved
    text: You've already solved this room! Head through the open door.
    duration: 3
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: fell
    text: Splash! Sump water is not a spa. Out you come.
    duration: 3
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: exit
    text: Pumps running, floor drying, Pebble ticking happily on the gauge. Lovely work, PIP.
    duration: 6
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: r1_hint_1
    text: 'Hint 1 of 4, the goal: open the door to the Gate Room. Its power comes from the cradle next to it, not from a socket.'
    duration: 7
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r1_hint_2
    text: 'Hint 2 of 4, the system: cradles take power cells. A cell only powers its cradle when all four bars are lit.'
    duration: 7
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r1_hint_3
    text: 'Hint 3 of 4, how they connect: you''re a power supply. Plug your Tether into the charge station and the cell in the station''s cradle fills up.'
    duration: 8
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r1_hint_4
    text: 'Hint 4 of 4, the action: plug in (right mouse / LT) until every bar glows green, unplug, carry the cell (E / X) to the door''s cradle and set it down.'
    duration: 9
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r2_hint_1
    text: 'Hint 1 of 4, the goal: open the gate and keep it open long enough to walk through.'
    duration: 6
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r2_hint_2
    text: 'Hint 2 of 4, the system: the gate hangs on a pulley. Weight in the pan lifts it, and the needle shows how much is in.'
    duration: 7
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r2_hint_3
    text: 'Hint 3 of 4, how they connect: anything you''re holding weighs nothing, and if you stand in the pan you''re not at the gate. It has to stay up without you.'
    duration: 8
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r2_hint_4
    text: 'Hint 4 of 4, the action: put both crates in the pan. The one on the high shelf comes down with a Tether pull.'
    duration: 7
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r3_hint_1
    text: 'Hint 1 of 4, the goal: lower the drawbridge, fetch Pebble from the far side, and carry Pebble to the tide gauge by the exit.'
    duration: 8
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r3_hint_2
    text: 'Hint 2 of 4, the system: the bridge works like the gate, with a pan. It also has a winch, and the winch cradle is a motor when it holds a full cell.'
    duration: 8
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r3_hint_3
    text: 'Hint 3 of 4, how they connect: there are two answers. A full cell in the winch cradle, or enough weight in the pan. The two crates alone aren''t quite enough. What else in here is heavy?'
    duration: 9
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: r3_hint_4
    text: 'Hint 4 of 4, the action: either charge the cell at the station and set it in the winch cradle, or put both crates AND the cell in the pan. Then cross, pick Pebble up, and set Pebble on the gauge.'
    duration: 10
    repeatable: 1
